2026-10-15 02:51:43,640 DEBUG: Chroma query output: {'ids': [['sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_3', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_2', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_23', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_20', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_15', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_0', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_11', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_10']], 'embeddings': None, 'documents': [['. This policy is effective as of April 1, 2025. While previous AI usage is not subject to the specific requirements herein, users are encouraged to review the policy, align their practices accordingly, and notify supervisors of previous AI usage. Definitions Artificial Intelligence (AI): A broad term encompassing any technique that enables computers to mimic human intelligence, such as problem-solving, learning, and decision-making', '. Scope and Applicability This policy applies to the use of any third-party or publicly available AI tools that mimic human intelligence to generate or analyze answers, create content, or perform certain tasks by faculty, staff, students, contractors and volunteers of Southeastern Louisiana University. For all research projects involving human participants, the project must still be reviewed according to Institutional Review Board policies and procedures', '. Additional Guidance For questions regarding the appropriate use of AI, please contact the Chief Information Officer at technology@southeastern.edu. Southeastern recognizes that AI technology is evolving rapidly. Therefore, this policy will be updated as needed. [End of Policy]', '. Personal Liability Faculty, staff, and students must oversee every decision or recommendation generated by AI to ensure its appropriateness, accuracy, and fairness. AI tools can assist with decision-making, but they lack the context, ethical considerations, and human judgments bring to complex scenarios. Faculty, staff, and students are accountable for all content created using AI. Users are responsible for the decisions that are based on that output', '. • While AI may be used to generate useful output, it lacks the context, ethical considerations, and human judgment and may introduce bias. Examples of tasks that AI should never be used for include, but are not limited to recruitment decisions, personnel decision making, disciplinary decision making, and grading decisions. • AI generated content may be misleading, inaccurate, or without proper attribution or permission', 'Responsible Administrator: CIO Responsible Office: Office of Technology Effective Date: 04/01/2025 Approved by: President Date of Revision: 11/07/2025 Artificial Intelligence Policy Policy Statement While artificial intelligence (AI) tools offer opportunities to streamline work functions and increase our productivity, they come with serious security, accuracy, and intellectual property risks', '. • Any use of AI should be disclosed in the work product whenever possible and appropriate. • Any use of AI where the AI is given access to data that could be considered PII, specific information about tangible or real property, proprietary information, confidential data, restricted data, or any information that would otherwise undermine the cybersecurity or physical security of the university will require review by the university ERP committee', '. Policy Procedure Requirements for Allowable Use of AI • For faculty, staff, student workers, graduate assistants, research assistants, contractors and volunteers, supervisors must be aware of any AI usage. • For students, AI usage must be consistent with course AI usage guidelines that are found in each course syllabus. • For faculty, the use of AI should follow all guidelines provided in the Semester Informational Memo provided by the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs']], 'uris': None, 'included': ['metadatas', 'documents', 'distances'], 'data': None, 'metadatas': [[{'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 3, 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy'}, {'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 2, 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/'}, {'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'index': 23}, {'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 20, 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docContext': 'sluPolicy'}, {'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 15, 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy'}, {'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'index': 0, 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy'}, {'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 11, 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy'}, {'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'index': 10, 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt'}]], 'distances': [[1.0355364084243774, 1.0635379552841187, 1.1465336084365845, 1.1638377904891968, 1.1688930988311768, 1.1884303092956543, 1.1893941164016724, 1.2256321907043457]]}

